  "bound_derivation": "Both the true and the truncated chain regenerate at the empty state and coincide until the first innovation that would exceed cmax (event F, time T*). With delta = E[T* 1_F] + K P(F), where K bounds the expected time to empty from any state (a block of length t with no innovation or encounter and a reset of both sites, probability exp(-(2 eta + 2 rho/b) t)(1-exp(-t))^2), every stationary probability differs by at most 2 delta / E[cycle] <= 2 alpha delta, alpha = 2 eta. P(F), E[T* 1_F] are solved on the truncated chain in floating point."
